## BLUF
1. **The defect (KS-1814, High, security, Backlog, no assignee, 0 comments):** `POST /api/documents/:id/anchor` (`services/originate/src/routes/documents.ts:1437-1571` at develop `ed12d4e08d43`) sits behind `authenticate()` (`documents.ts:175`) and tenant scoping only. Its sole state check is the 400 "Document is already anchored" at `:1458-1459`. No role gate, no owner or creator test, no terminal-status guard. Any authenticated tenant user, the public-signup `OWNER` role included, can make originate call the anchoring service for a document whose blob is absent or `anchor_failed`; each accepted anchor logs a Cardano fee (the ticket cites `fee 179449` lovelace in Seat D 42nd's demo log; whose wallet pays per box: UNMEASURED). On success the route writes `status: 'anchored'` through `updateDocument(id, tenantId, {...})` with no options, and `documentRepo.ts:598` / `:621-622` only keep `revoked` / `deleted` when `preserveTerminalStatuses` is true (default false), so a revoked document can be written back to `anchored`. Drafter confirmed all of this by reading the handler at `ed12d4e08d43`.
2. **The constraint that makes this a design item, not a one-line gate:** Platform S uses this route in its normal flow (KS-1688, Stuart's comment of 2026-10-19 23:36Z: "the anchor kick that follows it (`POST /{newId}/anchor`)", signed with the OWNING ORGANISATION's connector key plus `onBehalfOf`; and `/version` is called for watermark and sign-cert, so the anchored document is often a `/version`-minted child). A gate that refuses that principal turns S's anchors into 403s. Name the cell that proves it still works (QUEUE A.3).
3. **Your PR:** base develop on `Secuura/Distributed_Secuura`, opened under the project's board identity (the project `GH_TOKEN`, `kksecura`, per `/Volumes/DevMASTER/WEDNESDAY/2_Project_Files/fleet/STANDING_LINES.md`). Commit 1 = KS-1814 (fix + new red-first cells + both docs). Commit 2 = KS-1829's comment-only fix, nothing else. `Refs KS-1814` and `Refs KS-1829` in the body, never `Closes`. Tickets stay on their current assignee (all four read below are unassigned); you change no ticket's state or assignee.
