**Facts that bound the design (drafter's reading at `ed12d4e08d43`, to confirm):**
- A connector principal has `role === 'connector'` and `userId` = `connector:<platform>:<key-id>`, not a UUID (`utils/principalId.ts`). A document a connector made WITHOUT `onBehalfOf` has an EMPTY `owner.id`, so an owner-only test would refuse S's own documents; the creating connector is recognised only through `wasCreatedByConnector` (the GET read check carries this exact comment, KS-480 section 6).
- `/version` records `create:connector` on the document it mints (`documents.ts` ~`:2390-2397`, KS-1557 shape (a-prime)), so a `/version`-minted child IS recognised for its minter today. The KS-1688 sequencing warning ("gate only after KS-1557 lands") was written before this; confirm by a cell, do not assume (A.3, cell C6).
- Stuart's KS-1688 comment names ONE edge where S signs with a different key than the originating one: an S organisation merge (PS-492) re-homes documents to the surviving organisation, so a creating-connector test refuses that key. He offered two fixes and asked which K prefers; **that is unanswered on the board and is not yours to answer**. State in the PR that the predicate you chose refuses that edge (or does not), and why.
- The gateway mounts `/api/documents` with `requireScope('documents:read', 'documents:write')` (any ONE of them passes an OAuth or API-key caller; JWT and email users pass straight through, `middleware/scopes.ts`), so the gateway is no substitute for the check in originate. The gateway also has `blockPendingApproval` on this route (`routes/verification.ts:1028`).
