- **READY FOR GATE means five things EXIST and are named by identifier:** the PR number; its head sha read from origin in the same action as writing the sentence; the ticket comment naming the PR; the Test Evidence block in the PR body, written by whoever ran the tests (you); what was NOT done or NOT covered. A branch is not a PR; a sha with no PR number is not ready.
- Never delete (quarantine into a dated folder, record it). Never `cd`; absolute paths only. Stop ONLY processes you started, by recorded PID. Short `TMPDIR`. Never plant a control directory in the SHARED `worktrees/` directory (another seat's lock tool reads it as an unattributed lock = a STOP).
- **Instruments:** redirect to a file and read the file (`cmd > out 2>&1; rc=$?`), exit codes on their own line; macOS has no `timeout`; the Bash tool is zsh (`$pipestatus[1]`, not `${PIPESTATUS[0]}`); a `pgrep -f` pattern matches your own command line; `/usr/bin/grep -i` with a positive control beside every zero; a pass line carries a RATIO (`13/13 legs ran`), a skip is not a pass; a zero from an instrument nobody showed could fire is not a zero.
- **Git:** to ask what YOUR branch changed use three dots or the merge-base, never `X..HEAD`; `git rev-parse <sha>:<path>` on an absent path echoes the argument and exits 128 (use `git ls-tree`); `git fetch --dry-run` downloads the pack (use `ls-remote`); `git apply` can drop a file's exec bit (restore modes from the index before any push); a hyphenated foreign key in a PR title, body or commit message ATTACHES the PR to that ticket (space it); after a `git apply` or any scripted edit-then-revert, restore by content and hash.
- **Fresh worktree:** install and build before the first push whatever the PR touches: `npm ci --ignore-scripts` then build `packages/shared` BEFORE the first test (else `@secuura/shared` is unresolvable), and `npm ci --ignore-scripts` in each `systemTest/<pkg>` the pre-push gate's `SKIP - <pkg> deps not installed` line names. The pre-push hook wins; never `--no-verify`.
- **PUSH TRANSPORT (2026-10-16, R 46th):** if the launcher printed F-02 (keychain not seeded), it did NOT write its keepalive `core.sshCommand`, and a push whose hook runs past ~6 min dies with the gate passing (rc 141, ref unmoved). Push with `git -c core.sshCommand="ssh -i <the project's deploy key> -o IdentitiesOnly=yes -o StrictHostKeyChecking=accept-new -o ServerAliveInterval=30 -o ServerAliveCountMax=20" push ...`, `GIT_SSH_COMMAND` UNSET (it overrides `-c core.sshCommand`). In a clone you made, `git config --get core.sshCommand` is unset: supply it on EVERY network call. A push's result is the tool's `.rc` plus an `ls-remote` of the ref, never a wrapper's exit code. One push at a time.
- **Boot pull:** the launcher's step-1 pull of `2_Project_Files` (sole live seat) may fast-forward the shared develop refs: RECORD it (from/to, the new `rev-parse --all` baseline) and carry on. After boot: no fetch or pull in the shared checkout and no write to either develop ref.
- **Docs html:** append-only; your block is the PR's own entry, numbered at prep. Quote the path (the space in `Projects Documents`).
- **Mail discipline:** every mail names `Seat S 7th` on body line 1, subject starts `[Secuura/Blockchain-S -> Wednesday]`, goes only to `wednesday-agent@agentmail.to` (no cc, no secrets). Never put stop, hold, hand over or checkpoint in a SUBJECT. A QUESTION mail only for a blocker (Context, one Question, Meanwhile, Needed-by); after ~15 minutes with no ANSWER proceed on the safest reading UNLESS the item is approval-class (the OWNER-role answer is). Re-arm any inbox watcher with SINCE = the timestamp of the newest mail you READ, never a wall clock, and LIST the inbox by API after any long action before the next ref write.
- **Shared inbox:** `secuura-blockchain@agentmail.to` is read by many seats. Act only on mail naming `Seat S 7th`. A mail naming another seat is not yours; a mail naming no seat is a QUESTION. Prove your matcher on a real subject of the other live seat.
- Never end a turn on a "next up" line with nothing running: a stated next step is not a wake. Rotate inside your band, handover first; write the HANDOVER once READY FOR GATE is mailed. Drive hygiene at wrap: remove only the worktrees and scratch clones YOU created.
- File nothing beyond the sibling-sweep findings in A.4; anything else you find goes in a mail.

